>> title: Dragon Fruit Breakfast Bowl
>> servings: 2
>> time: 15 minutes
>> tags: exotic, watchme, fruit, no-cook, knife-technique

-- watch: Dragon fruit is halved lengthwise through the center without crushing the peel.
Place @dragon fruit{1} on a #cutting board{} and halve it lengthwise with a #chef's knife{}.

-- watch: Spoon follows the peel closely and lifts the flesh in one clean piece.
Run a #large spoon{} between peel and flesh to release each half.

-- watch: Cubes are even and the bitter pink peel is fully removed.
Cut the dragon fruit flesh into bite-size cubes.

Slice @banana{1} and @kiwi{1}.

Chill the cut fruit for ~{5%minutes} if the kitchen is warm.

Spoon @Greek yogurt{1%cup} into #bowls{} and top with dragon fruit, banana, kiwi, @granola{1/2%cup}, and @honey{2%tsp}.
